<title>USA: Italy's Ciampi says Stet to be sold off on time.</title>
<headline>Italy's Ciampi says Stet to be sold off on time.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-06-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian treasury minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi said there was no reason to believe Italian telecoms group Stet would not be sold off within an agreed timetable.</p>
<p>&quot;The intention is to respect the timetable. We are working in this direction and there is no reason to doubt that the timetable will be respected,&quot; Ciampi told reporters.</p>
<p>The government has said it intends to complete the sell-off of the telecoms giant by mid-October.</p>
<p>Ciampi was in Denver attending the Group of Seven summit of industrialized nations.</p>
</text>
